# Test fixtures.
# NOTE: this repo's Dockerfile runs `go mod download`, NOT `go mod tidy`, so the
# template's caution about stripping *_test.go does not apply here — tidy is
# what would resolve requirements from test files, and it never runs in-image.
**/testdata
**/*_test.go
# --- end managed ---
# Repo-specific entries below this line are preserved across regeneration.

# LOAD-BEARING — do not delete. The Dockerfile's builder stage overlays
# `COPY --from=ui /app/web/dist ./web/dist` so web/embed.go's `//go:embed
# all:dist` embeds freshly built assets rather than the tracked .gitkeep
# placeholder. A stale local web/dist leaking into the context would be copied
# in first and then shadowed — or worse, survive if the ui stage were skipped.
# The managed block's bare `dist` matches only a TOP-LEVEL dist, not web/dist.
# The Dockerfile's own comment points here.
web/dist

# The managed block's bare `node_modules` likewise matches only the top level;
# this repo's lives at web/node_modules.
**/node_modules

# Local build artifact — `go build ./cmd/stormglass` writes the binary to the repo root
/stormglass

